#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
TRACEATLAS MAPINT main.py
=========================

Public / authorized / evidence-first / safety-constrained mapping and
cartographic intelligence scaffold.

This module:
- Does NOT fetch live map services.
- Does NOT invent coordinates, boundaries, roads, buildings, routes, parcels,
  ownership, occupancy, facility function, or map features.
- Does NOT track private persons.
- Does NOT infer private homes from weak clues.
- Does NOT create stalking maps or personal routine maps.
- Does NOT provide evasion routing, checkpoint avoidance, border evasion,
  customs evasion, sanctions-evasion routing, or escape-route planning.
- Does NOT provide attack routes, strike coordinates, weapon-position
  optimization, facility-intrusion routing, sabotage chokepoints, or
  critical-infrastructure vulnerability exploitation.
- Does NOT generate actionable routes; it only validates supplied route
  references and network topology context.

It consumes deterministic map/GIS/cartographic records supplied by
authorized/public sources:
- map sources and pedigree metadata
- places, addresses, coordinates
- gazetteer/administrative context
- boundaries and administrative areas
- roads, railways, transit stops, ports, airports
- buildings, facilities, landmarks, POIs
- parcels, zones, land use, land cover
- hydrography, coastlines, waterways
- elevation/terrain layers where supplied as metadata or vector features
- historical maps and map versions
- supplied route references
- source reliability / independence / temporal validity metadata

It produces an evidence-linked MAPINTResult with:
- coordinate parsing and validation
- CRS / datum / projection metadata handling
- place/address/coordinate resolution status
- feature geometry validation
- topology checks
- containment / proximity / distance / area calculations where supported
- road-network topology context
- supplied-route validation without route generation
- historical map / change detection context
- source reliability / bias / pedigree / independence
- contradiction preservation
- competing hypotheses and falsification
- dual-AI style skeptic review
- privacy / safety flags
- graphical memory scaffold
- analyst summary and report-ready result object
"""

